cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the versioned software release."
title: "Genuine Zero Uniform Atlas Energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Massensini
    given-names: Thiago
license: MIT
version: 0.14.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the native real-camera/Genuine zero identity, the
  faithful C2--C7 cutoff operator, exact critical cutoff-tail jets, and the
  finite-to-limit transverse-energy architecture. Version 0.14.0 proves an
  exact crosswalk from the empirical cameras to the spectral-Weyl camera
  library, transports its all-order derivative-tail estimate, and derives an
  explicit six-camera finite second-jet bound with the M^(-3/2) log(M)^2
  rate. The identities use no supplied height and do not require simplicity;
  the existing quadratic coercivity route remains the multiplicity-one
  sector. The release does not promote the remaining denominator floors,
  fixed C/M constants, compact-region coverage, numerical evidence, or
  readout-domain equivalences to an unconditional confinement theorem.
keywords:
